+## Bounded adversarial review — review-f03127eed7712b25
+
+Source SHA-256: `0d16d2f73e50661626e30f3698d522a20e1be4b90fdf36d85347e7ea4e7b463d`.
+Canonical rule hash: `f2b6a399cf43`. No `evidence/review_index.json` was present.
+Production source was not changed. These are retained findings and repair
+proposals, not approval, a full battery, or a parametric construction.
+
+The public `Catalog.generate` API materialized 32 ordinary default lessons
+with three demonstrations and one query each (128 Racket-labeled pairs), seed
+0, no difficulty or content override. The catalog reports `not_reviewed_safe`;
+the explicit research option `allow_unapproved=True` is retained in the evidence.
+Each rival was fitted to demonstrations before testing query disagreement.
+
+| Rival | Lessons fitting all demos | Query disagreements after demo fit |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Component farthest toward bottom-right, by bbox bottom+right | 26 | 2 |
+| Component with rightmost bbox edge | 23 | 5 |
+| Minimum component bbox area | 32 | 0 |
+| Lowest component color index | 5 | 4 |
+
+Ties use ascending color, preserving row-major component order when still tied.
+The first finding for each of the three disagreeing rivals was replayed using
+both complete programs through protected Racket: 24 executions covering all
+demonstrations and the query. The original lessons and both candidate rules are
+retained privately in `WORK/checks/a4d31efd3a2f/probe.json`, so they can support
+the optional alternative-answer stream without reconstructing the lesson.
+
+Lesson 6 supports the lowest-color rival on all demonstrations, but its query
+requires the size-3 color-9 component rather than the size-7 color-2 component.
+Lesson 20 supports both positional rivals on all demonstrations, but its query
+requires a single color-8 cell rather than the bottom-right size-4 color-7 shape.
+That input also exposes overlapping placement: the larger color-8 polyomino is
+split into components of sizes 5 and 1 by the later painted shape. The generator
+therefore does not always maintain its advertised two disjoint blobs. Its
+current self-check counts colors and cannot detect this split. The canonical
